{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/pulls/158","id":5168467027,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUGncwM8AAAABNBCMUw","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/pull/158","diff_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/pull/158.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/pull/158.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/issues/158","number":158,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix HA catch-up for recurring root content with later publication cursors","user":{"login":"Franksudoman","id":273670192,"node_id":"U_kgDOEE_gMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/273670192?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman","html_url":"https://github.com/Franksudoman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Franksudoman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem\n\nHA root content can recur after intervening publications. The existing warm and cold selection paths treated equal content as current, then rejected a valid older local HA cursor at the mandatory exact-publication check. A stopped-node diagnostic from the df026 physical LAN run reached `current_cursor` failure with time still remaining and without entering replica installation. The log has no request identifier, so the source diagnosis does not invent a request correlation.\n\n## Change\n\nRequire both content and exact current cursor before the existing warm read fast path. The cold path also sends a covered but older same-content publication through the original full replica installer. Read-only witness continuation now requires an exact current persistent cursor before admission.\n\nThe strict `matches_current` check, original owner and ReadIndex, original request deadline, four-resource CAS, complete graph validation, and publication uncertainty handling remain intact. There is no cursor-only write path.\n\nAdd one independently counted real A→B→A regression with separate warm and cold local barriers. It checks that the old cursor remains covered but is not current, denies read-only continuation, verifies cursor/active pairing and retained history after installation, and cold-reopens both targets without another publication. Each request retains the original 15-second budget. Existing 60 normal tests and LAN 98+12 assertions are unchanged.\n\n## Exact source and validation\n\n- Sole parent: `6d02ceca629163e1c07480fa1f21520434407143`.\n- Candidate tree: `94ced21a63ff9aaca4538c0d4796efea2150e632`; independently rebuilt all 358 Merkle trees and 3,914 file leaves. Relative to the parent: 3 modified files, 1 new file, 3,910 unchanged, 0 deleted.\n- Actual pinned Rust 1.98.0 formatter: job `1a1aac9543c-fc05-4743`, exit 0, complete/durable output, 4 direct children reaped, original 50/10/60-second caps. All 18 fixed outputs independently read and whole-byte verified.\n- Root reviewed all actual formatter files, metadata and streams; formatting evidence tree `92fe1fa16ceb87d1741c95ba43e77a82dce3d7c6`.\n- New Rust compilation, Mac/Linux 60+1, and physical LAN regression are pending. Prior df026 host qualification does not transfer to this commit.\n\nThe original df026 LAN 91/98 and 0/12 failure, historical CI154 failures, and X230 unknown operation remain retained. This PR does not claim full OpenBao 2.7.1 replacement or authorize production cutover/old-version deletion.\n","created_at":"2026-11-05T08:26:15Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T08:26:15Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a3c0b9bc1aa6798e4b190424bfee8487a52c221d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/pulls/158/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/pulls/158/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/issues/158/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaBao/statuses/1c66541993662f92cf717154e33717abedb2ea74","head":{"label":"TrillionniumFoundation:codex/heptabao-same-root-publication-94ced21a-20261105-r1","ref":"codex/heptabao-same-root-publication-94ced21a-20261105-r1","sha":"1c66541993662f92cf717154e33717abedb2ea74","user":{"login":"TrillionniumFoundation","id":262513357,"node_id":"O_kgDOD6WizQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262513357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/repos","events_url":"http